Over a project tier holding two types, `ls` prints one line per record sorted by type name then
number, whatever order the files sit in: `{type}/{NNNN}  {status}  {summary}`, with `-` standing in
for a record that carries no `status` (values).

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/specs/value/0002-second.md --
---
type: value
title: Second
summary: The second value.
---
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/specs/value/0001-first.md --
---
type: value
title: First
summary: The first value.
---
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/specs/adr/0010-tenth.md --
---
type: adr
title: Tenth
summary: A later decision.
status: proposed
---
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/specs/adr/0002-second.md --
---
type: adr
title: Second
summary: An earlier decision.
status: accepted
---
-- cmd --
booping specs ls
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
adr/0002  accepted  An earlier decision.
adr/0010  proposed  A later decision.
value/0001  -  The first value.
value/0002  -  The second value.
-- stderr --
